{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02211",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.13,
      "end_seconds": 3.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Good morning, grab a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.96,
      "end_seconds": 8.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.11,
      "end_seconds": 16.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.84,
      "end_seconds": 23.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "absolutely, come and sit beside them. What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 25.03,
      "end_seconds": 33.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "It's a feeling of something stuck in my throat, doctor. She didn't want to to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.77,
      "end_seconds": 38.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.87,
      "end_seconds": 53.39,
      "duration_seconds": 13.52,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler. I take it once a day for my chest. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. Alendronate. I take it once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.24,
      "end_seconds": 58.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Alright, and and what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.32,
      "end_seconds": 60.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "It's 70 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.15,
      "end_seconds": 65.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.8,
      "end_seconds": 71.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Around two days... no wait, it's more like three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.43,
      "end_seconds": 76.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "How troublesome is it day to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.8,
      "end_seconds": 82.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "about a five out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.4,
      "end_seconds": 87.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Right, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.32,
      "end_seconds": 105.44,
      "duration_seconds": 16.12,
      "text": "A sharp scratch when swallowing goes along with it, most of the time. And I've been having eaten fish as well, for ten days. As for sharp scratch when swallowing, severe, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.23,
      "end_seconds": 114.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "Have you had a feeling of something stuck in your throat before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.55,
      "end_seconds": 125.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened a couple of years ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.18,
      "end_seconds": 130.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Have you had any blood or drooling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.74,
      "end_seconds": 133.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.0,
      "end_seconds": 138.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Have you had any neck swelling or difficulty breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.07,
      "end_seconds": 145.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "I haven't had neck swelling or difficulty breathing, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.12,
      "end_seconds": 150.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "alright, is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.84,
      "end_seconds": 153.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "no, my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.75,
      "end_seconds": 157.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.75,
      "end_seconds": 163.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I have COPD, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.43,
      "end_seconds": 165.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.31,
      "end_seconds": 169.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I have thin bones, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.34,
      "end_seconds": 177.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "yes, COPD and thin bones are known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.61,
      "end_seconds": 190.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.25,
      "end_seconds": 195.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.8,
      "end_seconds": 216.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.17,
      "end_seconds": 235.28,
      "duration_seconds": 18.11,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I've never smoked in my life. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I walk the dog every morning. No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.14,
      "end_seconds": 239.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.33,
      "end_seconds": 246.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "my father had bowel cancer my cousin has psoriasis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.97,
      "end_seconds": 249.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.66,
      "end_seconds": 253.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.36,
      "end_seconds": 272.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.83,
      "end_seconds": 286.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "okay, this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.98,
      "end_seconds": 307.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "okay: temperature 36.5, blood pressure 110 over 74, pulse 64."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.89,
      "end_seconds": 310.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.94,
      "end_seconds": 316.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.41,
      "end_seconds": 320.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.3,
      "end_seconds": 323.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.73,
      "end_seconds": 341.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "I can't see anything in the throat and the neck is not tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.6,
      "end_seconds": 360.91,
      "duration_seconds": 15.31,
      "text": "So, thank you, you can get dressed. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with a possible fish bone scratch or lodged bone at this stage. Another possibility is a pharyngeal scratch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.71,
      "end_seconds": 364.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.07,
      "end_seconds": 387.12,
      "duration_seconds": 21.05,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a possible fish bone scratch or lodged bone do well once it's treated properly. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had a feeling of something stuck in your throat for three days, and no difficulty breathing or neck swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.42,
      "end_seconds": 389.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.38,
      "end_seconds": 411.26,
      "duration_seconds": 20.88,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a neck X-ray for foreign body sensation. Sip water and eat soft foods; if it persists we look with a camera. We'll refer you to the ENT clinic. I'd like to see you again if still stuck tomorrow. Okay, that's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.47,
      "end_seconds": 415.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    }
  ]
}